==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[Gorkha]]

===Pronunciation===
{{wikipedia}}
*: {{rhymes|ɜː(r)kə}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A member of the dominant [[ethnic]] [[group]] in [[Nepal]], with a Himalayan diaspora
# A member of this people recruited to serve in their own elite units in the [[British]] and [[Indian]] [[army]]
# One of the seventy five districts of Nepal, located in the hilly region. Place of birth of the king Prithvi Narayan Shah, who is considered to be the founder of Nepal. Also home to the famous hindu temple, Manakamana Temple.

